-- הסכם עוז לתמורה (14.8.2011), §17 גמולים למורים בעלי תפקידים: from
-- תשע"ב, the allowance and the role hours of each role in the table — the
-- deputy principal, the grade, social-education, adjustments, subject and
-- measurement coordinators, the homeroom teacher, the educational
-- counsellor and the teacher the principal gives tasks; role hours the
-- employer may add from its own budget; the allowances that go on as they
-- were; the frontal hours a role holder still teaches; and the Ministry's
-- rules of appointment.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT parties
IMPORT vocabulary
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT `oz-founding-10`
IMPORT `oz-founding-38`
IMPORT `oz-founding-39`
IMPORT `oz-founding-41`

§ `17 גמולים למורים בעלי תפקידים`

DECLARE `Oz section 17 action` IS ONE OF
    `agree the complexity levels and the deputy principal's management allowance`
    `divide the deputies' management hours among them`
    `allot further management hours to a deputy principal`
    `use 3 individual hours for the adjustments coordinator's role`
    `allot role hours to a role holder this agreement gives none`

@desc A teacher holding a role under §17, with the facts the table's rows turn on.
DECLARE `Oz role holder` HAS
    `the role` IS A `Oz role`
    `a deputy on the eve of the reform, or first one in 5772 in a reform school` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (1)(א): deputy principal in his school on the eve of the reform there, or began as one in תשע"ב in a school applying it
    `the rate by the rules on the eve of the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc for a deputy under (1)(א), a subject coordinator outside English and mathematics (5%–7%) and an educational counsellor (5%–9%, counting no role hours in place of individual hours): the rate the collective agreements of 13.8.2011 give
    `coordinates English or mathematics` IS A BOOLEAN
    `coordinators of his subject` IS A NUMBER @desc the coordinators the school has for the subject he coordinates
    `classes in the school` IS A NUMBER
    `classes in his grade` IS A NUMBER @desc the grade a grade coordinator coordinates
    `classes in the upper division in his charge` IS A NUMBER @desc the classes an educational counsellor is responsible for
    `role hours the principal gives him` IS A NUMBER @desc a deputy's share of the deputies' management hours; a teacher's hours for the tasks the principal assigns; a subject coordinator's hours out of §41's basket

@desc The salary components a §17 allowance is computed on, at the teacher's own values; the 2011 and erosion supplements are §§38 and 39's, computed from these.
DECLARE `Oz role allowance base` HAS
    `the day`                     IS A DATE   @desc the day the allowance is paid for
    `the base by the rules on the eve of the signing` IS A NUMBER @desc the components the collective agreements of 13.8.2011 put in the allowance's base, together
    `the combined salary`         IS A NUMBER
    `the 1987 supplement`         IS A NUMBER
    `the 1994 supplement`         IS A NUMBER
    `the 2001 supplement`         IS A NUMBER
    `the 2008 supplement`         IS A NUMBER
    `the Oz LaTmura supplement`   IS A NUMBER @desc §16, or §28 in a year of part application

-- The 2011 supplement (§38) and the 2011 erosion supplement (§39) on the
-- teacher's own components, on the day.
GIVEN b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the 2011 supplement in the allowance base` b IS
    `the 2011 supplement under section 38` (b's `the day`) (b's `the combined salary`) (b's `the 2001 supplement`) (b's `the 2008 supplement`)

GIVEN b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the erosion supplement in the allowance base` b IS
    `the erosion supplement under section 39` (b's `the day`) (b's `the combined salary`) (b's `the 1987 supplement`) (b's `the 1994 supplement`) (b's `the 2008 supplement`) (b's `the 2001 supplement`)

@desc The role hours §17 gives a role holder, by the hours they take the place of (§10).
DECLARE `Oz role hours` HAS
    `in place of frontal hours`    IS A NUMBER
    `in place of individual hours` IS A NUMBER

§§ `17(א)`

-- (א): from תשע"ב, the allowances paid for a role to teachers employed on
-- the reform's terms (in full or in part) are as the table sets out, a row
-- per role: its allowance ("תגמול") and its role hours.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a akn:art_17__para_a/t1
GIVEN y IS A NUMBER, e IS A `extent of the Oz reform`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17's table sets the role allowances in` y e IF
        y AT LEAST `the school year 5772`
    AND NOT e EQUALS `off the Oz reform`

-- Rows 1, 2, 3, 5, 7 and 8 compute the allowance as the rules of the eve
-- of the signing did, and add to their base, "למען הסר ספק", the Oz
-- LaTmura supplement, the 2011 supplement and the 2011 erosion supplement.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_2__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_3__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_7__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_1
GIVEN b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the eve base with the Oz, 2011 and erosion supplements` b IS
      b's `the base by the rules on the eve of the signing`
    + b's `the Oz LaTmura supplement`
    + `the 2011 supplement in the allowance base` b
    + `the erosion supplement in the allowance base` b

-- Rows 4 and 6 name their base instead: the combined salary and the 1994,
-- 2001, 2008, 2011 erosion and Oz LaTmura supplements. The 2011 supplement
-- is not in it, though §38(ג) (`the 2011 supplement under section 38 counts
-- for`) brings it into every percentage supplement on the combined salary
-- save five that are not role allowances; the erosion supplement, which
-- §39(ב) brings in the same way, the rows do list (F-oz-founding-17-a). The
-- reading adopted (convention precedence.specific): the row's own list,
-- which speaks of this allowance.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_4__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_6 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_6/p1
GIVEN b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the base rows 4 and 6 list` b IS
      b's `the combined salary`
    + b's `the 1994 supplement`
    + b's `the 2001 supplement`
    + b's `the 2008 supplement`
    + `the erosion supplement in the allowance base` b
    + b's `the Oz LaTmura supplement`

GIVEN r IS A `Oz role`, b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 17 allowance base` r b IS
    IF r EQUALS `the Oz adjustments coordinator` OR r EQUALS `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator`
    THEN `the base rows 4 and 6 list` b
    ELSE `the eve base with the Oz, 2011 and erosion supplements` b

§§§ `17(א) סגן מנהל בית ספר`

-- (1)(א): a deputy principal who was one on the eve of the reform in his
-- school, or began as one in תשע"ב in a school applying it, is paid a
-- percentage allowance by the rules of the eve of the signing (the rate an
-- input), on the base above.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_1
GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deputy keeps the eve rules' allowance` h IF
    h's `a deputy on the eve of the reform, or first one in 5772 in a reform school`

-- (1)(ב): any other deputy is paid a management allowance by the
-- complexity level set for his school. The parameters of the level and the
-- allowance for each are for the parties to agree by 5 Tevet 5772
-- (31.12.2011, the day included: convention dates.end), the summary to be
-- annexed as annex ד'. The agreement the corpus publishes carries no annex
-- ד' (its annexes are א'–ג', ה' and ו'): the allowance is set elsewhere.
-- (The steering committee's decision of 28.5.2013, §7, gives such a deputy
-- the (1)(א) allowance until the parties agree otherwise; not encoded yet.)
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_1__cls_b
`why a deputy's management allowance under (1)(ב) has no figure here` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "סיכום הצדדים על הפרמטרים לקביעת רמת המורכבות של בית הספר ועל גמול הניהול של סגן המנהל לפיה, שיצורף כנספח ד' להסכם (עד 31.12.2011)"

`days from the Oz signing to 31.12.2011` MEANS
    DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 31 12 2011) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 14 8 2011)

`agreeing the deputies' complexity levels` MEANS
    (PARTY `the employer`
     MUST  `agree the complexity levels and the deputy principal's management allowance`
     WITHIN `days from the Oz signing to 31.12.2011`
     LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "§17(א) סגן מנהל (1)(ב): the complexity levels and the deputy's allowance are agreed by 31.12.2011")
    RAND
    (PARTY `the secondary teachers' organisation`
     MUST  `agree the complexity levels and the deputy principal's management allowance`
     WITHIN `days from the Oz signing to 31.12.2011`
     LEST  BREACH BY `the secondary teachers' organisation` BECAUSE "§17(א) סגן מנהל (1)(ב): the complexity levels and the deputy's allowance are agreed by 31.12.2011")

-- (2)(א): all the school's deputies together are given 0.5 weekly role
-- hours times the number of classes in the school, divided among them by
-- the principal as the school needs, in place of frontal hours (§9), so
-- long as each deputy still teaches 9 frontal hours a week (in fact).
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_a
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the management hours of all the deputies` classes IS
    0.5 TIMES classes

`dividing the deputies' management hours` MEANS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MUST  `divide the deputies' management hours among them`

-- (2)(ג): an employer may give a deputy further management hours in place
-- of his frontal hours, if (1) they are paid from budgets the State did not
-- allot, (2) the frontal hours the school's timetable sets for teaching the
-- curriculum do not fall for it, and (3) the deputy still teaches 9 frontal
-- hours a week. The conditions are cumulative (convention reading.lists).
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_c akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_c__pnt_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_c__pnt_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_c__pnt_3
GIVEN `paid from budgets the State did not allot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the frontal hours the deputy would still teach` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Oz section 17 action`
DECIDE `giving a deputy further management hours` `paid from budgets the State did not allot` `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall` `the frontal hours the deputy would still teach` IS
    IF      `paid from budgets the State did not allot`
        AND `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall`
        AND `the frontal hours the deputy would still teach` AT LEAST `the frontal hours a role holder teaches at least` `the Oz deputy principal`
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MAY   `allot further management hours to a deputy principal`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- (2)(ד): in תשע"ב the fit of the deputies' management hours to the
-- system's needs is to be checked, and no change made under the section may
-- raise the agreement's cost. The clause puts the check on no one, so no
-- duty is encoded; the bound on the cost is.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_d
`the deputies' management hours are checked in` MEANS `the school year 5772`
`a change to the deputies' management hours may raise the agreement's cost` MEANS FALSE

§§§ `17(א) רכז שכבה`

-- The grade coordinator of grade י', י"א or י"ב, or of grade ט' in a
-- four-year school (§2).
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_2
GIVEN grade IS A NUMBER, `a four-year school` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a grade an Oz grade coordinator may coordinate` grade `a four-year school` IF
        (grade AT LEAST 10 AND grade AT MOST 12)
    OR  (grade EQUALS 9 AND `a four-year school`)

-- (1): 6% (with the other rates, below). (2): a coordinator of a grade of
-- 4 classes or more ("ומעלה": 4 is in) is given 1 weekly role hour per
-- class in the grade, 12 at most; half in place of frontal hours, the rest
-- in place of individual hours — no more than his position holds ("למען
-- הסר ספק") — so long as he still teaches 12 frontal hours a week.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_2__subpara_2
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a grade coordinator's role hours` classes IS
    IF classes AT LEAST 4
    THEN min classes 12
    ELSE 0

§§§ `17(א) רכז חינוך חברתי`

-- (2): 0.4 role hours per class in the school, in place of frontal hours,
-- so long as he still teaches 12 frontal hours a week.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_3 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_3__subpara_2
GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a social-education coordinator's role hours` classes IS
    0.4 TIMES classes

§§§ `17(א) רכז התאמות`

-- (2): he may use 3 individual hours to do the role.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_4 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_4__subpara_2
`using individual hours for the adjustments role` MEANS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `use 3 individual hours for the adjustments coordinator's role`

`the individual hours the adjustments coordinator may use for the role` MEANS 3

§§§ `17(א) רכז מקצוע`

-- (1)(א): in English and mathematics 9%; where a subject has several
-- coordinators, the rate is divided among them equally. (1)(ב): in the
-- other subjects 5% to 7%, by the teachers and weekly hours in his charge
-- and the rules of the eve of the signing (the rate an input). "5% עד 7%"
-- is a range and 7% is in it (an exception to convention thresholds.until).
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5__subpara_1__cls_b
GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rate a subject coordinator outside English and mathematics may have` r IF
    r AT LEAST 5% AND r AT MOST 7%

-- (2): his role hours are §41's (which applies to every teaching
-- employee): what the principal allots him out of the subject
-- coordinators' basket, an hour at most, in place of frontal hours.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5__subpara_2
GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a subject coordinator's role hours` h IS
    `the role hours section 41 gives a subject coordinator` (h's `role hours the principal gives him`)

§§§ `17(א) מחנך כיתה`

-- (2): 3 role hours in place of frontal hours (§9).
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_7 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_7__subpara_2
`a homeroom teacher's role hours` MEANS 3

§§§ `17(א) יועץ חינוכי`

-- (1): 5% to 9% by the rules of the eve of the signing (the rate an input;
-- 9% is in the range, as above); the role hours in place of individual
-- hours are not counted in computing it. (2)(א): 1.7 weekly hours per class
-- in his charge in the upper division, in place of frontal hours, so long
-- as he still teaches 8 frontal hours a week; (ב): all the individual
-- hours.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_2__cls_b
GIVEN r IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rate an educational counsellor may have` r IF
    r AT LEAST 5% AND r AT MOST 9%

GIVEN classes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an educational counsellor's role hours` classes IS
    1.7 TIMES classes

§§§ `17(א) משימות שיוטלו על-ידי המנהל`

-- Role hours the principal gives a teacher out of the basket of role hours
-- the Ministry allots the school, in place of frontal hours (§9); no more
-- than four weekly hours to one teacher ("לא יעלה על": 4 is in). No
-- allowance.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_9 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_9/p1
`the most role hours for tasks the principal assigns` MEANS 4

§§§ `17(א) the allowances`

-- Each row's rate: (1)(א) the deputy's by the eve rules, 6% for the grade,
-- social-education, adjustments and measurement coordinators, 9% (shared)
-- or 5%–7% for a subject coordinator, 10% for a homeroom teacher, 5%–9% for
-- an educational counsellor, and none for the tasks the principal assigns.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_1__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_2__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_3__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_4__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_5__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_6/p1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_7__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_9/p1
GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 17 allowance rate` h IS
    CONSIDER h's `the role`
    WHEN `the Oz deputy principal` THEN
        IF `the deputy keeps the eve rules' allowance` h
        THEN JUST (h's `the rate by the rules on the eve of the signing`)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `the Oz grade coordinator` THEN JUST (6%)
    WHEN `the Oz social-education coordinator` THEN JUST (6%)
    WHEN `the Oz adjustments coordinator` THEN JUST (6%)
    WHEN `the Oz subject coordinator` THEN
        IF h's `coordinates English or mathematics`
        THEN JUST (9% DIVIDED BY max 1 (h's `coordinators of his subject`))
        ELSE JUST (h's `the rate by the rules on the eve of the signing`)
    WHEN `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator` THEN JUST (6%)
    WHEN `the Oz homeroom teacher` THEN JUST (10%)
    WHEN `the Oz educational counsellor` THEN JUST (h's `the rate by the rules on the eve of the signing`)
    WHEN `the Oz teacher with tasks the principal assigns` THEN JUST 0
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- The allowance: its rate times its base. NOTHING where §17 sets none: a
-- deputy under (1)(ב) (set elsewhere), and a role the table does not name.
GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`, b IS A `Oz role allowance base`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the section 17 role allowance` h b IS
    CONSIDER `the section 17 allowance rate` h
    WHEN JUST rate THEN JUST (rate TIMES `the section 17 allowance base` (h's `the role`) b)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

§§§ `17(א) the role hours`

-- The role hours each row gives, in place of the hours §10 says they
-- replace, kept within the frontal hours the role holder must still teach
-- ((ד) and the rows' own floors) and within the individual hours his
-- position holds. The week is §10's: the role hours stand where the hours
-- they replace stood; the subject coordinator's are §41's; a role the
-- table gives no hours, none. (2)(ב) of the deputy's row, and (2)(ב) of
-- the counsellor's: all the individual hours.
@ref akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_1__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_17__para_a__hc_2__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_3__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_7__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_2__cls_a akn:art_17__para_a__hc_8__subpara_2__cls_b akn:art_17__para_a__hc_9/p1 akn:art_17__para_d
GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`, w IS A `Oz work week`
GIVETH A `Oz role hours`
DECIDE `the role hours section 17 gives` h w IS
    CONSIDER h's `the role`
    WHEN `the Oz deputy principal` THEN hours (h's `role hours the principal gives him`) individual
    WHEN `the Oz grade coordinator` THEN
        hours (half (`a grade coordinator's role hours` (h's `classes in his grade`)))
              (min (half (`a grade coordinator's role hours` (h's `classes in his grade`))) individual)
    WHEN `the Oz social-education coordinator` THEN hours (`a social-education coordinator's role hours` (h's `classes in the school`)) 0
    WHEN `the Oz subject coordinator` THEN hours (`a subject coordinator's role hours` h) 0
    WHEN `the Oz homeroom teacher` THEN hours `a homeroom teacher's role hours` 0
    WHEN `the Oz educational counsellor` THEN hours (`an educational counsellor's role hours` (h's `classes in the upper division in his charge`)) individual
    WHEN `the Oz teacher with tasks the principal assigns` THEN
        hours (min (h's `role hours the principal gives him`) `the most role hours for tasks the principal assigns`) 0
    OTHERWISE hours 0 0
    WHERE
        individual MEANS w's `individual hours with pupils`
        room MEANS max 0 (w's `frontal teaching hours` MINUS `the frontal hours a role holder teaches at least` (h's `the role`))
        half n MEANS n DIVIDED BY 2
        hours f i MEANS `Oz role hours` WITH
            `in place of frontal hours`    IS min f room
            `in place of individual hours` IS i

GIVEN h IS A `Oz role holder`, w IS A `Oz work week`
GIVETH A `Oz work week`
DECIDE `the Oz week of a role holder` h w IS
    `the hours left besides the role hours` w (r's `in place of frontal hours`) (r's `in place of individual hours`)
    WHERE
        r MEANS `the role hours section 17 gives` h w

§§ `17(ב)`

-- (ב): an employer may give a role holder whom this agreement gives no
-- role hours role hours in place of his frontal hours, if (1) they are paid
-- from budgets the State did not allot, (2) the frontal hours the timetable
-- sets for teaching the curriculum do not fall for it, and (3) no teacher
-- is given more than four weekly hours so. Cumulative (convention
-- reading.lists).
@ref akn:art_17__para_b akn:art_17__para_b__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_b__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_b__subpara_3
GIVEN `paid from budgets the State did not allot` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the role hours given him so` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Oz section 17 action`
DECIDE `giving role hours to a role holder the agreement gives none` `paid from budgets the State did not allot` `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall` `the role hours given him so` IS
    IF      `paid from budgets the State did not allot`
        AND `the timetable's frontal hours do not fall`
        AND `the role hours given him so` AT MOST 4
    THEN PARTY `the employer`
         MAY   `allot role hours to a role holder this agreement gives none`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `17(ג)`

-- (ג): besides (א)'s, these allowances go on, on the rules the collective
-- agreements set for them on the eve of the signing: the profession and
-- training allowance, special education, bagrut preparation, the split
-- allowance, the assistant to a boarding school's security coordinator,
-- and the security coordinator. A closed list (convention
-- reading.closed-list).
@ref akn:art_17__para_c akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_1 akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_2 akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_3 akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_4 akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_5 akn:art_17__para_c__subpara_6
DECLARE `allowance section 17(ג) keeps` IS ONE OF
    `the Oz profession and training allowance`
    `the Oz special-education allowance`
    `the Oz bagrut-preparation allowance`
    `the Oz split allowance`
    `the Oz allowance of a boarding school's assistant security coordinator`
    `the Oz security coordinator's allowance`

`the allowances section 17(ג) keeps` MEANS
    LIST `the Oz profession and training allowance`, `the Oz special-education allowance`, `the Oz bagrut-preparation allowance`, `the Oz split allowance`, `the Oz allowance of a boarding school's assistant security coordinator`, `the Oz security coordinator's allowance`

`section 17(ג)'s allowances keep the rules of the eve of the signing` MEANS TRUE

§§ `17(ד)`

-- (ד): a role holder teaches at least 12 frontal hours a week (in fact),
-- unless the parties agreed otherwise. The table's rows set their own
-- floors — 9 for a deputy, 8 for an educational counsellor, 12 for the
-- grade and social-education coordinators — and for those rows it is
-- theirs that bind (convention precedence.specific): the parties agreed
-- otherwise in the agreement itself.
@ref akn:art_17__para_d
GIVEN r IS A `Oz role`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the frontal hours a role holder teaches at least` r IS
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the Oz deputy principal` THEN 9
    WHEN `the Oz educational counsellor` THEN 8
    OTHERWISE 12

§§ `17(ה)`

-- (ה): who may be appointed to a role is the Ministry of Education's
-- guidelines', as they are from time to time.
@ref akn:art_17__para_e
`why the rules of appointment to a role are not here` MEANS
    `set elsewhere` "הנחיות משרד החינוך בדבר כללי המינוי לתפקידים, כפי שיהיו מעת לעת"

§§ `17 -- illustrations`

GIVEN r IS A `Oz role`, classes IS A NUMBER, grade IS A NUMBER, given IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Oz role holder`
DECIDE `an Oz role holder of` r classes grade given IS
    `Oz role holder` WITH
        `the role` IS r
        `a deputy on the eve of the reform, or first one in 5772 in a reform school` IS TRUE
        `the rate by the rules on the eve of the signing` IS 6%
        `coordinates English or mathematics` IS FALSE
        `coordinators of his subject` IS 1
        `classes in the school` IS classes
        `classes in his grade` IS grade
