-- F-oz-founding-17-a's evidence: §38(ג) brings the 2011 supplement into
-- the percentage supplements on the combined salary; between 1.9.2011 and
-- 1.1.2012 it grows from 2.25% to 4% (the erosion supplement stays at
-- 2.1%), and for the adjustments and measurement coordinators that moves
-- nothing in the base, where for the homeroom teacher (and the other rows)
-- it does.
`rows 4 and 6 leave the 2011 supplement out of their base` MEANS
        `the 2011 supplement under section 38 counts for` `computing another percentage supplement on the combined salary`
    AND `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz adjustments coordinator` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.1.2012`)
            EQUALS `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz adjustments coordinator` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.9.2011`)
    AND `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.1.2012`)
            EQUALS `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz measurement and evaluation coordinator` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.9.2011`)
    AND NOT `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz homeroom teacher` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.1.2012`)
            EQUALS `the section 17 allowance base` `the Oz homeroom teacher` (`an allowance base of 10,000 on` 10500 `1.9.2011`)
#ASSERT `rows 4 and 6 leave the 2011 supplement out of their base`
